//@version=1
/* The requests tour: every request.security capability of the static
   slice in one script. The primary axis comes from examples/primary.csv
   (synthetic prices on real weekday timestamps); every requested series
   is real, fetched live through the built-in source registry. */
indicator("Requests tour")

len = input.int(10, "Child smoothing", minval=1)

// An unprefixed symbol resolves through the yahoo default. The captured
// expression runs with its own state INSIDE the child context (an ema over
// SPY's closes, not ours), and the input param crosses in — bind-time
// params are compilation-global.
spy = request.security("SPY", "D", ta.ema(close, len))

// History on a merged result is parent-row-indexed: the previous ROW of
// this chart, whatever child bar served it.
spyStep = spy - spy[1]

// Explicit prefix routing, weekly bars served natively by the driver,
// gaps on — rows between weekly closes stay na instead of carrying
// forward.
qqqWeekly = request.security("YAHOO:QQQ", "W", close, gaps=true)

// A bogus symbol under ignore_invalid_symbol: the column is na, never a
// bind error.
ghost = request.security("ZZZZZZZZ", "D", close, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)

// FRED macro data (single-valued source: the value serves as close).
// Monthly CPI month-over-month change sampled onto this daily axis; the
// value changes only when a new monthly observation lands. Without
// FRED_API_KEY in the environment the column is na (ignore_invalid_symbol
// covers the typed configuration error).
cpi = request.security("FRED:CPIAUCSL", "M", ta.change(close), ignore_invalid_symbol=true)

// DYNAMIC requests: the symbol is a series — a different context per row.
// Each distinct pair resolves once, on first encounter (Pine v6
// dynamic_requests, default on).
rotate = request.security(bar_index % 2 == 0 ? "SPY" : "QQQ", "D", close)

plot(spy, title="SPY ema10")
plot(spyStep, title="SPY ema step")
plot(qqqWeekly, title="QQQ weekly close")
plot(ghost, title="ghost")
plot(cpi, title="CPI m/m")
plot(rotate, title="SPY/QQQ rotate")
